  <language>en_US</language>
  <keyword>nansum</keyword>
  <short_description>Sum, ignoring NaN values.</short_description>
  <syntax>
    <syntax_item>y = nansum(X)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>y = nansum(X, dim)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>y = nansum(X, vecdim)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>y = nansum(X, 'all')</syntax_item>
  </syntax>
  <description>
    <p><b>nansum</b> computes the sum after removing <b>NaN</b> values from each operated slice; a slice made only of <b>NaN</b> sums to <b>0</b>.</p>
    <p>The default operating dimension is the first nonsingleton dimension.</p>
    <p>It is equivalent to <b>sum(X, ..., 'omitnan')</b>.</p>
  </description>
  <examples>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description />
      <example_item_data runnable="cli"><![CDATA[y = nansum([1 NaN 3 NaN 5])]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
  </examples>
